---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/');
const issues = 'https://github.com/incompl/pudding/issues';
---
<Page title="Support — Pudding" description="Get help with Pudding, report a bug, or suggest an improvement directly to the project’s developer.">
  <header class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Let’s keep the music playing</p><h1>Support<span class="primary">.</span></h1><p class="intro">Pudding is an independent project by Greg Smith. Questions, bug reports, and thoughtful feedback are welcome.</p></header>
  <div class="support-options">
    <article><h2>Find your way around.</h2><p>Start with the guide for installation, your music library, radio stations, playlists, and keyboard shortcuts.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${base}documentation/`}>Read the documentation <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article>
    <article><h2>Something off-key?</h2><p>Check existing GitHub issues for a similar problem, or open a new one to report a bug, ask a question, or discuss an idea. A GitHub account is required to post.</p><a class="text-link" href={issues}>Questions &amp; feedback on GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article>
  </div>
  <div class="prose policy">
    <section><h2>A useful bug report includes</h2><ul><li>Your macOS version and Pudding version or source revision.</li><li>What you were doing, what you expected, and what happened instead.</li><li>The steps needed to reproduce the problem, and any error message.</li><li>For playback issues, the audio file format or the public station URL.</li></ul><p>GitHub issues are public. Leave out private file paths, personal information, and private stream URLs. Pudding does not send automatic diagnostics, so the details you choose to share help us understand the problem.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Privacy questions</h2><p>Read the <a href={`${base}privacy/`}>privacy policy</a> for how Pudding handles local files and radio connections. You can contact Greg through the <a href={issues}>project’s issue tracker</a> with questions about the policy.</p></section>
  </div>
</Page>
